Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":9,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":30,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["sobek"],"visibility":"public","forks":9,"open_issues":30,"watchers":284,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Brief summary\n\nTypedArray.set does not respect subarray offset (or just ignores subarrays and uses original array).\nIt breaks libraries like protobufjs.\n\nSeems to be related to grafana/k6#5226\n\n### k6 version\n\nk6 v1.3.0 (commit/devel, go1.25.1, darwin/arm64)\n\n### OS\n\nmacOS 15.6.1\n\n### Docker version and image (if applicable)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to reproduce the problem\n\n```\nexport default function test() {\n  const slab = new Uint8Array(4)\n  const arr = slab.subarray(1, 4);\n  console.log(...arr, \" - \", ...slab);\n  arr.set([1,2,3], 0);\n  console.log(...arr, \" - \", ...slab);\n}\n```\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\n```\n0 0 0 ' - ' 0 0 0 0\n1 2 3 ' - ' 0 1 2 3\n```\n(from Google Chrome console)\n\n### Actual behaviour\n\n```\nINFO[0000] 0 0 0  -  0 0 0 0                             source=console\nINFO[0000] 2 3 0  -  1 2 3 0                             source=console\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/sobek/issues/99/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/sobek/issues/99/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":20917620611,"node_id":"CE_lADOAz4Wr87QWylXzwAAAATeyY-D","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grafana